class_name VignetteFigures
## Frame layout of the vignette footballer sheets (assets/vignette/figures_*.png).
## GENERATED by ard-asset-pipeline (tools/combine_sheets.py) - rebuild, don't edit by hand.
##
## figures_shade.png:  R lighting, G hair weight, B shorts weight, A coverage.
## figures_mask.png:   R guernsey base colour (guernsey + socks), G sock band, B skin, A guernsey alone.
## figures_design.png: (DESIGN_SCALE: 2 half size, 1 full) R across the guernsey, G up it,
##                     B front/back - for club designs.
## Boots take the weight left over. Each body's moves are strips: one per animation and
## facing ("front" faces the camera; "back" shows the number; "back_r" is three-quarters
## from behind, heading right; "side_l" nearly side-on, heading left; "front_r" three-
## quarters from the front, heading right - mirror a frame for the other way). A strip's
## frames sit left to right from (x, y), each `size` pixels (cropped to the move's figures,
## so strips differ in size). pivot: the feet in the strip's frames, pixels. reach: per
## frame, the figure's highest point above its feet, metres (a leap's hands). contact: the
## middle of the boots' contact with the turf over the strip, pixels - where his shadow
## centres (the pivot is under his ankles; the boots reach forward of it). markers: the
## frames where something happens (foot_plant_l/r, ball_release, ball_contact, gather_contact,
## mark_secure), measured from the rig. Numbers are printed on the guernsey by the shader
## (figures_digits.png), not placed here.

